<section class="sx" id="text">
  <div class="container">
    <article class="legal">
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: 12 October 2026</p>

      <p>
        This policy explains how Conservation Trips &amp; Adventures ("we", "us") handles personal
        information when you use this website or contact us about a trip. We have tried to keep it
        short and in plain language.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Conservation Trips &amp; Adventures is a travel, tourism and conservation management company
        based in Uganda.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Address: 8FF4+GH3 Kyanyanya Trading Center, LUKAAWA PLAZA, Buloba, Busiro county, Uganda</li>
        <li>Email: <a href="mailto:info@tripsandadventures.co.ug">info@tripsandadventures.co.ug</a></li>
        <li>Phone / WhatsApp: <a href="tel:+256767936590">+256 767 936 590</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Enquiry details you give us</strong> — your name, email address, phone number,
          country, the trip you are interested in, travel dates, group size, and anything you write
          in the "requirements" or "message" box (for example dietary or accessibility needs).
          Please only share health information if it is needed to plan your trip.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Messages you send us</strong> by email, phone or WhatsApp.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Technical data</strong> that your browser sends automatically when you visit any
          website (such as your IP address and browser type), which our hosting provider and the
          third-party services listed below may log.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To reply to your enquiry and prepare an itinerary and quotation.</li>
        <li>
          To arrange and deliver a trip you decide to book — for example reserving lodges, transport
          and guides, and applying for park or gorilla permits, which can require names and passport
          details.
        </li>
        <li>To keep records we are required to keep, and to protect against fraud or misuse.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use it for advertising profiling.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
      <p>This website does not set advertising or tracking cookies. It stores two small items in your browser:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>cookiesAccepted</strong> (local storage) — remembers that you dismissed the cookie notice.</li>
        <li><strong>toastShown</strong> (session storage) — stops the "permits are limited" reminder appearing more than once per visit.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You can clear these at any time in your browser settings.</p>

      <h2>Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        To load the site we use content from other providers. When your browser fetches it, that
        provider receives your IP address and may set its own cookies under its own policy:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Font Awesome via cdnjs, and flag icons via jsDelivr (icons)</li>
        <li>Google Maps (the map on the Contact page)</li>
        <li>WhatsApp (when you choose to chat with us, you leave this site and are subject to WhatsApp's terms and privacy policy)</li>
        <li>Social networks, if you follow a link to our profiles there</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If the enquiry form is configured to use a hosted form service, your enquiry passes through
        that service on its way to us. Otherwise the form opens a prepared email in your own email
        app, and nothing is sent until you press Send.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        Only with people who need it to deliver your trip — such as lodges, drivers and guides, and
        park or wildlife authorities when permits are required — and with service providers who help
        us run the business, under appropriate confidentiality. We may also disclose information if
        the law requires it.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep enquiries for as long as needed to deal with them and, if you travel with us, for
        the period we need for accounting, legal and safety records. After that we delete or
        anonymise them.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask us to tell you what we hold about you, correct it, delete it, or stop
        contacting you, and you can withdraw consent you have given us. Write to
        <a href="mailto:info@tripsandadventures.co.ug">info@tripsandadventures.co.ug</a> and we will
        respond within a reasonable time. We aim to handle personal data in line with applicable law,
        including Uganda's Data Protection and Privacy Act, 2019.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This website is intended for adults planning travel. If you are booking for a family, please
        give us information about children only as far as is needed for the trip.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we change how we handle information we will update this page and the date above.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy? Email
        <a href="mailto:info@tripsandadventures.co.ug">info@tripsandadventures.co.ug</a> or
        <a href="/contact">use the contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
